  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Dengue Incidence in Indonesia through Wolbachia Technology Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The investment supports the World Mosquito Program (WMP) in reducing the transmission of dengue in Bali, Indonesia, by using Wolbachia technology. This initiative builds on WMP&#x2019;s successful trial in Yogyakarta, which achieved significant reductions in dengue cases and hospitalizations. In partnership with Save the Children (STC) and Yayasan Kerti Praja, the program will release mosquitoes carrying Wolbachia, a naturally occurring bacteria in Denpasar, aiming to establish long-lasting community protection against dengue. Activities include setting up production facility, capacity building, community awareness campaigns, and technology transfer for mosquito eggs production and diagnostics. This investment will also complement Indonesia&#x2019;s Ministry of Health &#x201c;Five Cities&#x201d; Wolbachia Program.</narrative>
  </description>
